  <content>
  <section><para class="os-raise-text-bold">Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</para>
<para>For 1 - 4 use the problem below:</para>
<blockquote>Priya is buying raisins and almonds to make trail mix. Almonds cost $5.20 per pound, and raisins cost $2.75 per
  pound. Priya spent $11.70 buying almonds and raisins. The relationship between pounds of almonds, pounds of raisins,
  and the total cost is represented by the equation \(5.2a+2.75r=11.7\).</blockquote>
<para>How many pounds of raisins did Priya buy if she bought the following amounts of almonds?</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>2 pounds of almonds</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>
    a.
    1.192
  </item>
  <item>
    b.
    2.75
  </item>
  <item>
    c.
    0.946
  </item>
  <item>
    d. 0.473
  </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis> 0.473</para>
<para>\(5.2(2) + 2.75r = 11.7\)
  \(10.4 + 2.75r = 11.7\)
  \(10.4 + 2.75r - 10.4 = 11.7 - 10.4\)
  \(2.75r = 1.3\)
  \((1/2.75) (2.75r) = (1/2.75) (1.3)\)
  \(r = 0.473\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>1.06 pounds of almonds</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>
    2.25
  </item>
  <item>
    1.689
  </item>
  <item>
    5.5
  </item>
  <item>
    2.811
  </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis> 2.25</para>
<para>\(5.2(1.06) + 2.75r = 11.7\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>0.64 pounds of almonds</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>9.94
  </item>
  <item>1.911
  </item>
  <item>3.044
  </item>
  <item>8.371
  </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>3.044</para>
<para>\(5.2(0.64) + 2.75r = 11.7\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(a\) pounds of almonds</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>\(r=\frac{11.7+5.2a}{2.75}\) </item>
  <item>\(r=\frac{11.7-2.75a}{5.2}\)
  </item>
  <item>\(r=\frac{2.75}{11.7-5.2a}\) </item>
  <item>\(r=\frac{11.7-5.2a}{2.75}\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis>  \(r=\frac{11.7-5.2a}{2.75}\)</para>
<para>\(5.2(a) + 2.75r = 11.7\)</para>

<para>For 5 - 6 use the problem below:</para>

<blockquote>A car traveled 180 miles at a constant rate.</blockquote>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item> For each of the missing spaces in the table, a-d, select the missing value that
    completes the table to show the rate at which the car was traveling if it
    completed the same distance in each number of hours.</item>
</list>
<table class="os-raise-skinnytable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
        Travel Time
        (Hours)
      </entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
        Rate of Travel
        (Miles Per Hour)
      </entry>
    </row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>5</entry>
      <entry>a. ____ </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>4.5</entry>
      <entry>b. ____ </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>3</entry>
      <entry>c. ____ </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>2.25</entry>
      <entry>d. ____ </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>

<para><emphasis>CHOICES: </emphasis></para>
<list>
  <item>40</item>
  <item>80</item>
  <item>36</item>
  <item>60</item>
</list>
<para>a. ____ </para>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis>36</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    <para>b. ____</para>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 40</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    <para>c. ____ </para>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 60</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    <para>d. ____</para>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 80</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item>Choose the equation that would make it easy to find the rate at which the car
    was traveling in miles per hour \(r\), if it traveled for \(t\) hours.</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>\(r=\frac t{180}\)</item>
  <item>\(r=\frac{180}t\)</item>
  <item>\(r=180t\)</item>
  <item>\(r-180-t\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis>  \(r=\frac{180}t\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item> Bananas cost $0.50 each, and apples cost $1.00 each. <emphasis>Select all three</emphasis> combinations of bananas
    and apples that Elena could buy for exactly $3.50.</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>2 bananas and 2 apples</item>
  <item>3 bananas and 2 apples</item>
  <item>1 banana and 2 apples</item>
  <item>1 banana and 3 apples</item>
  <item>5 bananas and 2 apples</item>
  <item>5 bananas and 1 apple</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> “3 bananas and 2 apples” and “1 banana and 3 apples” and “5 bananas and 1 apple”</para>
<para>\(3(0.5)+2(1)=3.50\)
  \(1(0.5)+3(1)=3.50\)
  \(5(.5)+1(1)=3.50\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="8" type="enumerated">
  <item>Choose the best answer to solve the formula \(A=P+Prt\) for \(t\).</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>\(t=\frac{P-A}{Pr}\)</item>
  <item>\(t=\frac{A-P}{Pr}\)</item>
  <item>\(t=\frac{A+P}{Pr}\)</item>
  <item>\(t=\frac{r(A-P)}P\)</item>
  
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis>  \(t=\frac{A-P}{Pr}\)</para>
<para>\(A=P+Prt\)
  \(A-P=P-P+Prt\)
  \(A-P=Prt\)
  \(\frac{A-P}{Pr}=\frac{Prt}{Pr}\)
  \(\frac{A-P}{Pr}=t\)</para></section>
